In the public context, because a call relayed in by the proxy is not one
FreeSWITCH has authenticated and vanilla puts those here. 9000 answers and
plays the built-in stream, so the lab needs no sound files of its own; hold and
resume need nothing at all, since mod_sofia handles the re-INVITE itself.
-->
<include>
  <!-- Bridged to a loopback leg rather than answering and playing on its own.
       A channel that answers by itself is a one-legged call, and mod_sofia
       refuses to transfer one: "Cannot Blind Transfer 1 Legged calls", and
       "Cannot transfer channels that are not in a bridge". There has to be
       somebody on the other side to hand over. -->
  <extension name="sipral_lab">
    <condition field="destination_number" expression="^9000$">
      <action application="bridge" data="loopback/9002/public"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>
  <!-- the far side of that bridge. A cadenced tone: 1200 ms of sound, 600 ms
       of silence, repeating.

       The cadence is the point and it was not there. A de-jitter buffer gives
       back the delay it grew over an interruption only in a pause — dropping a
       frame during speech is audible and dropping one in silence is not — so a
       far end that never stops speaking means every measurement over an
       impaired link is taken against a buffer stuck where the worst moment
       left it. Measured before this: twenty seconds through an eight-second
       outage ended at 420 ms of delay where a clean run of the same length sat
       at 20 ms.

       An echo would be better still, because then "audible" would prove our
       own audio made the round trip rather than that this end is generating
       some. It was tried here and does not survive the loopback bridge: eight
       packets came back out of a hundred and two.

       Not local_stream://moh either: music on hold needs the sound files and a
       profile configured to serve them, and when it is missing playback fails
       and the channel hangs up half a millisecond after the ACK — which still
       looks like a call that connected, and is how it went unnoticed. -->
  <extension name="sipral_lab_media">
    <condition field="destination_number" expression="^9002$">
      <action application="answer"/>
      <action application="playback" data="tone_stream://%(1200,600,350,440);loops=-1"/>
      <action application="hangup"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>
  <!-- somewhere for a transfer to go. A different tone, so a capture says
       which leg is which without reading the SDP -->
  <extension name="sipral_lab_transfer">
    <condition field="destination_number" expression="^9001$">
      <action application="answer"/>
      <action application="playback" data="tone_stream://%(60000,0,480,620)"/>
      <action application="hangup"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>
  <!-- 8.5.1's RFC 4733 DTMF flow. `read` collects one digit into a channel
       variable however it arrived on the wire, and `send_dtmf` names it
       straight back — as a telephone-event, since rfc2833-pt is this
       profile's own setting in lab_profile.xml and send_dtmf uses whichever
       method the endpoint is configured for. `silence_stream://1` in place
       of a prompt file: one millisecond of nothing, so the digit is read
       without a tone playing over it. -->
  <extension name="sipral_lab_dtmf">
    <condition field="destination_number" expression="^9003$">
      <action application="answer"/>
      <action application="read" data="1 1 silence_stream://1 digit 5000 #"/>
      <action application="send_dtmf" data="${digit}"/>
      <action application="hangup"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>
  <!-- DTLS-SRTP (RFC 5764), the same number Asterisk gives it. Secure media
       made mandatory for this call alone, before the answer, so an offer
       this end could not key is refused rather than answered in the clear;
       the call is then the cadenced tone of 9002, played by this leg itself
       since nothing is transferred on it. -->
  <extension name="sipral_lab_dtls">
    <condition field="destination_number" expression="^9005$">
      <action application="set" data="rtp_secure_media=mandatory"/>
      <action application="answer"/>
      <action application="playback" data="tone_stream://%(1200,600,350,440);loops=-1"/>
      <action application="hangup"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>
  <!-- A far end that holds, resumes and refreshes a call keyed by SDES on
       its own, for the harness's farhold flow. Only AES_CM_128_HMAC_SHA1_80
       is taken, so an offer that lists AEAD_AES_256_GCM first is answered on
       its second line. That holds only on the lab_late profile
       (lab_late_profile.xml), which Kamailio sends 9010 to: there the offer
       is read once the call is answered, after the suite is set below. On
       the lab profile the offer is read as the INVITE arrives, the first
       line FreeSWITCH can run is taken before this extension says anything,
       and the suite set here then refuses the call it already chose. Two
       seconds after the answer FreeSWITCH holds the call
       (a re-INVITE with a=sendonly), three seconds later resumes it, and
       three seconds after that re-offers it as it stands; each re-INVITE
       carries its own a=crypto lines, which this end answers with the key of
       the line in force. The call itself is an echo, so audio coming back
       after each re-offer is this end's own audio having made the round trip
       under the keys both ends hold. No loopback leg here, unlike 9000: the
       echo does not survive that bridge, and nothing is transferred. -->
  <extension name="sipral_lab_far_hold">
    <condition field="destination_number" expression="^9010$">
      <action application="set" data="rtp_secure_media=mandatory:AES_CM_128_HMAC_SHA1_80"/>
      <action application="answer"/>
      <!-- sched_api is an API command, not a dialplan application: it is
           run by expanding it, which schedules the command and returns -->
      <action application="set" data="far_hold=${sched_api(+2 none uuid_hold ${uuid})}"/>
      <action application="set" data="far_resume=${sched_api(+5 none uuid_hold off ${uuid})}"/>
      <action application="set" data="far_refresh=${sched_api(+8 none uuid_media_reneg ${uuid})}"/>
      <action application="echo"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>
</include>
